+// A context's security token (0039): which contexts of an isolate V8 lets reach into each other.
+//
+//   int32_t Ssrs2_SetSecurityToken(int32_t context, const uint16_t* token, int32_t length);
+//
+// V8 gives every context a security token, by default the context's own global object, so that no two contexts
+// have the same one, and refuses a few operations made from one context on another whose token is not the same
+// object. Ssrs2_SetSecurityToken gives the context (its number, 0032, or 0 for the current one) a token of the
+// host's: a string (UTF-16, length characters, which may be 0), made a unique string of the isolate, so that two
+// contexts given the same characters have the same token and two given different characters do not. token null
+// gives the context its default token back. It answers the context's number, 0 with no isolate entered on this
+// thread, a number that names no context, or a negative length. It may be called at any time and again (V8 compares
+// the tokens at each operation, not once); nothing else of the context changes.
+//
+// What V8 15.6 asks the tokens for (the context "asking" is the one entered: the context of the script the host
+// started, or of Ssrs2_CallIn, not the realm of the function that makes the call):
+//   - the Function constructor of another context, and its generator, async and async generator forms, called,
+//     constructed, bound or given to Reflect.construct: a TypeError ("no access") without the same token, also
+//     when the call is made by a function of that other context which the asking context called;
+//   - the global eval function of another context: undefined is answered, nothing compiled;
+//   - the Promise constructor of another context given an executor that is not of that context: a TypeError;
+//   - another context's global object itself: reading, writing, defining or deleting a property of it, `in`, a
+//     property's descriptor and setting its prototype are a TypeError, and its keys are answered as none. Ordinary
+//     objects, functions and prototypes of another context are never asked about: a script that holds one reads,
+//     writes and calls it whatever the tokens (a script function is called with another context's global as its
+//     `this` too).
+// A token does nothing to a context's check of code generation (0019, 0032): once the tokens let a call through to
+// another context's Function constructor or eval, V8 asks the check of the context that constructor or eval belongs
+// to, with that context's number, as for a call from inside it; the calling context's own check is not asked.
+// Threading: the isolate's thread, the isolate entered and locked by the caller. No script runs and no callback is
+// made: safe inside any host call or callback.
+NATIVE_ENTRY_POINT(int32_t) Ssrs2_SetSecurityToken(int32_t context, const uint16_t* token, int32_t length) noexcept
+{
+    auto isolate = v8::Isolate::TryGetCurrent();
+    if (isolate == nullptr || (token != nullptr && length < 0))
+    {
+        return 0;
+    }
+    v8::HandleScope scope(isolate);
+    auto target = Ssrs2Contexts::Find(isolate, context);
+    if (target.IsEmpty())
+    {
+        return 0;
+    }
+    if (token == nullptr)
+    {
+        target->UseDefaultSecurityToken();
+    }
+    else
+    {
+        // (a unique string: V8 compares tokens as objects, and equal characters are then one object)
+        v8::Local<v8::String> made;
+        if (!v8::String::NewFromTwoByte(isolate, token, v8::NewStringType::kInternalized, length).ToLocal(&made))
+        {
+            return 0;
+        }
+        target->SetSecurityToken(made);
+    }
+    return Ssrs2Contexts::NumberOf(isolate, target);
+}
+
 // String arenas (0029): text an embedder and a context's scripts both read without copying it at each crossing. An
 // arena is blocks of memory that never move; an entry is a string's characters, one byte each when all are Latin-1,
